"""AletheiaTelos DealFlow Engine - restart-safe seed data.

Why this exists: the Render free tier gives the app an ephemeral SQLite
database, so every service restart wipes the pipeline. This module bakes the
43 curated nationwide listings (LoopNet research, 2026-09-24) into the
application itself. `seed_database()` runs at boot (see wsgi.py) and restores
the pipeline on every start.

Rules honored here (same as everywhere else in this repo):
  - The listed cap rate is evidence, not an input. It is recorded in the
    deal notes only. NOI is never derived from a listed cap rate; it stays
    missing until verified financials are supplied.
  - The 4 home-run deals (Wendy's 200-350 bps buy-below-market rule, approved
    2026-09-24) are seeded directly to PURSUE; the other 39 seed as NEW.
    (Seed-time status assignment, not a human transition.)
  - Idempotent: a deal is skipped when a record with the same
    name + location or the same source_url already exists, so re-seeding
    never duplicates - even with several gunicorn workers booting at once
    (a process-wide file lock serializes them).
"""

